# Optional. Unset, droidread uses a local SQLite file at ~/.droidread/chats.db
# and nothing ever leaves the machine.
#
# Set these to sync the index to a Turso cloud database instead. The auth token is a
# real credential: keep it in .env (gitignored), never in a committed file.
# TURSO_DATABASE_URL=libsql://<your-db>.turso.io
# TURSO_AUTH_TOKEN=<token>

# Path to adb, if it isn't on PATH.
# DROIDREAD_ADB=/home/you/Android/Sdk/platform-tools/adb

# Override where extracted data is stored (default: ~/.droidread)
# DROIDREAD_HOME=/home/you/.droidread

# MCP over the network (mcp/http.ts). All optional; without a token the HTTP server
# refuses to start, and without DROIDREAD_MCP_HOST it binds to 127.0.0.1 only.
#   echo "DROIDREAD_MCP_TOKEN=$(openssl rand -hex 32)" >> ~/.droidread/.env
# DROIDREAD_MCP_TOKEN=<64 hex chars>
# DROIDREAD_MCP_HOST=127.0.0.1,10.20.0.7      # comma-separated; prefer VPN interfaces over LAN
# DROIDREAD_MCP_PORT=7373

# The web viewer (web/server.ts) already captures frames whenever a browser is watching.
# Point droidread at it and screenshots cost the phone nothing — no second adb screencap
# competing with a read in progress. Unset, screenshots use adb directly.
# DROIDREAD_STREAM_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8791
# DROIDREAD_STREAM_MAX_AGE_MS=1500          # how stale a reused frame may be
# DROIDREAD_WEB_PORT=8791                   # viewer listen port (HTTPS twin on port+1)
